    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The technical picture for JPM is genuinely bullish \u2014 price at $189.70 sits just -0.18% from its 60-day peak with positive returns across all timeframes (+4.34% 5-day, +8.74% 20-day, +13.58% 60-day), full bullish moving-average alignment (price above 10 EMA, 50 SMA, and 200 SMA), and an expanding MACD histogram. The fortress balance sheet ($4.09T assets, $336.6B equity) supports holding. However, the rally is running on below-average volume (relative volume 0.72), RSI at 66.27 signals exhaustion risk after a +10.4% vertical recovery, and price is 4.4% above the 20-day SMA \u2014 a level that has historically preceded mean reversion for JPM. Critically, there is NO income statement, macro, news, or sentiment data in this historical window to confirm the fundamental strength that would justify a high-conviction BUY at a 52-week high. Conversely, there is no evidence of deterioration to justify a SELL. The balanced evidence supports maintaining the position without adding aggressively. For existing holders, I recommend holding with a protective stop below the 50 SMA (~$181.50), and consider trimming 10-20% into strength near the upper Bollinger band ($191.99) to lock in gains. For new money, wait for a pullback toward the 10 EMA ($185.31) or 50 SMA ($182.91) for a better entry, or for fundamental confirmation before initiating.\n\n**Entry Price**: 185.31\n\n**Stop Loss**: 181.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; consider trimming 10-20% into strength near upper Bollinger band ($191.99). New money: wait for pullback to 10 EMA ($185.31) or 50 SMA ($182.91).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
